 "_comment": "Threat (aggro), restart the server after editing. Every point of damage a player deals adds damageMultiplier threat (auto-attacks, skills, damage-over-time ticks), times their class's multiplier. Some skills also add flat threat every cast (dataThreat: the Grimoire's table by rank). A monster turns to whoever gets above switchMargin times its current target's threat (1.1 = 10% more). skills: flatThreat replaces the data's flat threat for that skill at every rank (null = the data's, 0 = none); multiplier scales the skill's flat threat and the threat from its hits (1 = unchanged, 2 = double, 0.5 = half; Taunt and Warcry: their damage-as-threat). A DoT's ticks use the multiplier of its status effect id, listed by that id. Being more than 50 levels above a monster still cuts all threat to 10%.",
